\ Regression: a code_ptr-less first-class quotation written in qmod calls
\ `head`, a word qmod imported with `use "cons-list"`. qmod-run tail-calls
\ report-error in another module, popping qmod's deps frame, and report-error
\ runs the quotation there. Under --emit-runtime-image the quotation stays
\ code_ptr-less and runs through the interpreter, which resolves `head` against
\ the loaded runtime image, so the quotation raises the real index-out-of-bounds:
\ of `head` on an empty list rather than failing with unknown-word.

use "./support/qmod.1z" ;

qmod-run
